# PROBE different-individuals. r is functional with r(c, a) and r(c, b), so a = b, which a ≠ b contradicts.
# construct: DifferentIndividuals
# expect: inconsistent

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:r a owl:FunctionalProperty .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual . :b a owl:NamedIndividual . :c a owl:NamedIndividual .
:c :r :a .
:c :r :b .
:a owl:differentFrom :b .
